      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found that the reason I wasn\u0027t seeing the compile failure on EC is because BoringSSL was [setting `-DXOPEN_SOURCE\u003d700`](https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/f94f3ed3965ea033001fb9ae006084eee408b861/CMakeLists.txt#208). There\u0027s actually a bug in our EC BoringSSL build where we\u0027re not setting `CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME` to `Generic`, which is why we were hitting that path.\n\nFrom the [`strdup` manpage](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/strdup.3.html) it looks like  `_XOPEN_SOURCE \u003e\u003d 500` or `_POSIX_C_SOURCE \u003e\u003d 200809L` needs to be defined in order to have `strdup`. Since BoringSSL is using `strdup`, it should be adding one of those in its own `CMakeLists.txt`, similar to what it does [here](https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/f94f3ed3965ea033001fb9ae006084eee408b861/CMakeLists.txt#208). Can you push this change upstream to BoringSSL?",
